{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1497352-albrecht-sword","id":1497352,"title":"Albrecht sword.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-17T05:00:57-08:00","id":1497352,"title":"Albrecht sword.","content":"I am curious and I seek Your help - forum users. <br /> In Ahroun chapter of Chronicles of Apocalypse there's Jacob Morningkill klaive mentioned.<br /> Albrecht is searching for it to destroy it. <br /> At the same time king Albrecht have scimitar like klaive named Solemn Lord.<br /> My question is - is it the same sword? If not how he get Solemn Lord and from who? If yes what's Your opinion about keeping it by Albrecht instead of destroying?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T11:37:02-08:00","id":1497383,"title":"","content":"There's nothing to suggest Jacob's unnamed-in-the-books klaive is the same as Solemn Lord. We don't know how Jonas got Solemn Lord, but he had it before his exile, and managed to retain it despite that. Jacob's weapon is also described as a standard sized klaive, while Solemn Lord is explicitly a grand klaive.<br /> <br /> Given how the Silver Fangs operate, Jonas most likely got Solemn Lord at a point earlier in his life than when we meet him in the books (aka his exile days) as a family heirloom for some act done during his younger adventures before falling out of grace with the Morningkills.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T12:13:24-08:00","id":1497391,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Albrecht is in early editions wielding klaive, not the grand one. In first tribebook he is both with klaive (inside book) and withe grand klaive (back cover). I wonder what happened with his first klaive or it is just artist interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T12:17:20-08:00","id":1497392,"title":"","content":"Given there's zero mention of him having two klaives, I would call that artistic interpretation (esp. as Solemn Lord wasn't detailed until later).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T14:22:12-08:00","id":1497415,"title":"","content":"I always thought the big one was Solemn Lord, and that the early illustation was just artistic depictions of Solemn Lord before the Timbrook one became the go to model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-18T02:17:18-08:00","id":1497448,"title":"","content":"Well, i would ask myself at what point of Albrecht's narrative he acquires the facial battle scar and sword, because that back cover image is, afaik, the first depiction of <b>both</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-18T02:47:45-08:00","id":1497450,"title":"","content":"I always thought that he get the scar during Silver crown story novel. But I don't remember losing eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-20T09:47:25-08:00","id":1497635,"title":"","content":"Going back to the original 1e corebook, we have the famous fight scene between Albrecht and Mari Cabrah that occurred over the many pages discussing Actions. This was later repeated in the 2e and W20 corebooks as well (though not Revised).<br /> <br /> In those illustrations, we see the Albrecht already has a klaive, though not a Silver Sword (what would be called a Grand Klaive later on). And we see that it is Mari that damages Albrecht's left eye (you can see that specifically on page 287 of the W20 corebook). Presumably Albrecht wanted to keep the Battle Scar and never healed it, perhaps to remind himself or Mari of their battle. Perhaps even to honor her fighting prowess.<br /> <br /> We don't see that wound in the 2e corebook comic book by Tony DiTerlizzi though it is obvious that Albrecht has already had a violent encounter with Mari before. There are some strange markings near Albrecht's right eye which might be scars, or it could be some kind of tattoo. It is hard to tell with DiTerlizzi's art style. If we want to take everything in that comic as strictly accurate, then Albrecht healed his eye after the original battle and then received damage to it again. However, I think it is more likely DiTerlizzi just didn't draw things accurately because he didn't know the entire backstory or that the fight illustrations were canon. Or assumed it got healed (explaining the scars around the eye), but accidentally got which eye wrong. Or that after it DiTerlizzi created his comic, the White Wolf staff decided to make it canon and insisted going forward any Albrecht illustration carry the eye wound from Mari.<br /> <br /> If we wanted to reconcile everything, we could say Mari severely damaged Albrecht's face and damaged his eye, but that vision loss was slight at that point. By the time he runs into Evan, his vision is still fairly good (in the comic he is initially wearing glasses and since it is night time, these have to be normal eyeglasses, not sunglasses). He kept the damage as a Battle Scar. However, as time progressed the vision in his eye continued to deteriorate and he eventually lost it entirely.<br /> <br /> In the W20 character creation example, we get &quot;Bill&quot; (presumably Bill Bridges) creating Albrecht. There we learn that he spent four Freebies to obtain a klaive as a reminder of his grandfather's favor. We are also told that as part of his back story before character creation &quot;He's spent a while as a homeless drunk in New York City, self-destructively provoking other werewolvesinto fighting him, including Mari Cabrah, a Black Fury who gave as good as she got.&quot;<br /> <br /> Based on that, I would say Albrecht originally did not have the grand klaive Solemn Lord, but a normal ancestral klaive from House Morningkill. He lost his eye to Mari either in the initial battle or over time because wounds suffered then. He obtained the grand klaive Solemn Lord later on. Perhaps he has given away his original klaive to some other deserving Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}